ID cards are also attendance cards — the number on the card is the **RFID** on the person's record,
which is what makes their scans register. So a lost card is an attendance problem, not just an
identity one.

**You need:** access to **Administration → ID Cards**.

## The blank card pool

The pool is the stock of unissued cards. Add cards to it as you receive them from your supplier; the
screen tells you what is left. Issuing draws from this pool, so an empty pool is why issuing fails.

## Card designs

Under **Card designs**, upload your institute's design as a PDF — separately for **Student card**
and **Teacher card**. This is held for reference, so whoever prints has the right artwork; the
printed card itself is produced from it.

**Upload PDF** adds one, **Replace** swaps it, and removal is immediate (**Card design removed**).

## Replacing a lost card

1. Open **Administration → ID Cards** and choose **Report a lost card**.
2. Pick **Student** or **Teacher**.
3. Enter the **Student ID** or **Teacher ID**.
4. Select **Issue Temporary Card**.
5. **Print** the card.

The temporary card carries a new number, and that number becomes the person's active RFID. Their old
card stops working — which is the point, since it is presumably in someone else's hands.

## If someone's attendance stops working

Check their card before anything else. The two usual causes are a lost card that was never reported,
so scans are going to a dead number, and a record that never had an RFID filled in at all — see
[Add a Student](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student).

